/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.l8KjQg/inputs/d1-subtree-review-grok46-20260902.md:228:`d1floor.achievable` implements (UNI) correctly: `N=k V_2 q` with `k V_2<=u` and `N in Z`. CONTROL 5 **prints a different formula**, `N=k·numerator(q)` for `k=1..floor(u/den(q))`, which is `N=t q` for `den(q)|t<=u` and **drops `V_2`**. That check is display-only: the only `check()` in CONTROL 5 is `U=u q`. The 232 384 skeleton controls therefore did not catch it.
