    93	Let `Lambda(delta)=sum_j min(delta, ord(tau_i-tau_j))` along `tau_i`'s path (self-term `=delta`). For `delta<delta^0` one has `lambda_g^{tau}(delta)<0`, so `Lambda(delta)=ord_t((g-c_2)(sigma_delta))=lambda_g^{tau}(delta)`. Continuity: `Lambda(delta^0)=0`. Generic `c_2` makes the leading form of the frontier ball have simple roots (FRONTIER-N, INT16 PROMOTED): no two shifted roots have contact `>delta^0`. Hence `min(delta^0, ord(tau_i-tau_j))=ord(tau_i-tau_j)` for `j≠i`, and
    94	
